From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shyalya <shyalya@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 07:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Healing Touch followed a pointer to an expired aura

spell_druid_healing_touch::OnFinish walks spell->m_appliedMods and reads
mod->ownerAura->GetId(). That pointer is captured when the modifier is
applied; if the aura expires while the spell is still in flight, it points at
freed memory.

Crash of 2026-08-06 at 00:05, with this = 0x73657220666c6573. Read as bytes
that is "self res" - a string from the playerbot module had taken over the
aura's memory. A second crash at 07:03 gave 0x6966206469706172, "rapid fi".

SpellModifier carries the id itself, and the constructor sets spellId from
that very aura, so the field is exactly equivalent and the pointer need not
be touched at all. The same applies to the SpellEntry, which the spell
manager can hand over by id.

These were the only two live dereferences of ownerAura in the tree. The three
in Player.cpp have been commented out for a long time, which suggests someone
walked into this before.
---
diff --git a/src/scripts/spells/spell_druid.cpp b/src/scripts/spells/spell_druid.cpp
index d0d971d..686ae43 100644
--- a/src/scripts/spells/spell_druid.cpp
+++ b/src/scripts/spells/spell_druid.cpp
@@ -342,16 +342,22 @@ struct spell_druid_healing_touch : public SpellScript
             return;
 
         int32 refundPct = 0;
+        // ownerAura is a raw pointer captured when the modifier was applied.
+        // If the aura expires while the spell is still in flight it points at
+        // freed memory - on 2026-08-06 it held a string from the playerbot
+        // module. spellId carries the same id and is set from that very aura
+        // in the constructor, so the field is enough and the pointer stays
+        // untouched.
         for (SpellModifier const* mod : spell->m_appliedMods)
         {
-            if (!mod || !mod->ownerAura)
+            if (!mod)
                 continue;
 
-            switch (mod->ownerAura->GetId())
+            switch (mod->spellId)
             {
                 case SPELL_DRUID_AESSINAS_BLOOM_BUFF_RANK_1:
                 case SPELL_DRUID_AESSINAS_BLOOM_BUFF_RANK_2:
-                    if (SpellEntry const* bloomInfo = mod->ownerAura->GetSpellProto())
+                    if (SpellEntry const* bloomInfo = sSpellMgr.GetSpellEntry(mod->spellId))
                         refundPct = std::max(refundPct, bloomInfo->CalculateSimpleValue(EFFECT_INDEX_0));
                     break;
                 default:
